## `tools/awscc2cdk/src/naming.ts`

Not a copy or adaptation of any upstream file — it is a from-scratch algorithm described in its
own header as "inspired by ideas from" `spec2cdk/naming/conventions.ts`'s sanitizers (which live,
adapted, in `sanitizers.ts` above) and cdk-terrain's `uniqueClassName` (which it deliberately
replaces with a different, deterministic algorithm). No third-party copyright header applies;
it is covered by this package's own MPL-2.0 root license like the rest of cdktn-io's original
code.

## `generated/` — the 1,494 emitted resource bindings

Every `.ts` file under `generated/` (per-resource files and per-module/root `index.ts` barrels;
not the `.jsiirc.json`, `MANIFEST.sha256`, `scope-map.effective.json` or `package.exports.json`
metadata, which are plain data with no comment syntax or authorial content) now carries:

    // Copyright (c) cdktn-io
    // SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0

**Reasoning, and why this is not "Copyright IBM Corp." / "Copyright (c) HashiCorp, Inc.":**
cdktn-io/cdktn-provider-awscc (a sibling, hand-generated-by-cdktn provider package) stamps
"Copyright IBM Corp. 2021, 2026 / SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0" on every generated file. That
header is *not* emitted by cdk-terrain's provider-generator itself — confirmed by reading
`tools/awscc2cdk/src/vendored/cdktn/provider-generator.ts`, which only ever writes
`// generated from terraform resource schema`, no copyright line — it is stamped afterward by that
repo's own `copywrite` tool (`.copywrite.hcl`, `license = "MPL-2.0"`), which applies the project's
declared license/copyright header project-wide, generated output included, without distinguishing
authored from generated files.

Copying that IBM/HashiCorp attribution onto *our* generated/ tree would misattribute authorship:
`generated/` here is the output of this package's own generator
(`tools/awscc2cdk/src/grouped/**`), which is a heavily-adapted derivative of cdk-terrain's
generator, not a copy of it (see `src/grouped/README.md` for what changed structurally: grouped,
namespace-qualified, `Cc`-prefixed aws-cdk-lib-shaped output instead of cdk-terrain's flat
per-resource-directory output). The emitted text — class/interface names, property lists, JSDoc —
is newly authored by running that adapted tool over public schema data (the awscc Terraform
provider schema, itself derived from AWS CloudFormation's public resource-type schemas); no
upstream source text is copied into it. So the header identifies the actual author (cdktn-io) and
the actual license the combined output is distributed under (this package's own MPL-2.0), while
still following the *precedent* cdktn-provider-awscc set — that generated Terraform CDK bindings
should carry a copyright + SPDX header at all, in that two-line `//` shape (matching the style
already used throughout this codebase's hand-written MPL headers, rather than the `/** */` block
form cdktn-provider-awscc's copywrite tool happens to emit).

The header is emitted by `tools/awscc2cdk/src/grouped-generate.ts` (the only code path that writes
to `generated/`; `src/legacy-generate.ts` — the unmodified-vendored-generator path used only by the
step1 golden/parity test — is unchanged and untouched by this audit).

## Modification-note convention

Per Apache-2.0 §4(b) and MPL-2.0 §3.4(a), every adapted (not byte-identical) vendored file states
what changed, either in its own header (short adaptations) or via a pointer to a longer writeup
(`tools/awscc2cdk/src/vendored/VENDORED.md`, `tools/awscc2cdk/src/grouped/README.md`,
`tools/lazify/VENDORED.md`) for adaptations too long to summarize in a header comment. Byte-
identical vendored files carry the upstream header/notice with no modification note, since none
occurred (verified by diffing against the pinned-commit origin — see the VENDORED.md tables).

## Third-party dependencies

Ordinary npm dependencies (jest, typescript, jsii, aws-cdk-lib, etc.) are not vendored — they are
installed via `pnpm` and carry their own licenses under `node_modules/`, unrelated to this NOTICE.
